---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Loft Conversion Huntingdon | Truleum Cambridgeshire Specialists"
  description="Expert loft conversion services in Huntingdon, Cambridgeshire. Local team for dormer, Velux and hip to gable loft builds across Huntingdon and nearby towns."
>

  <main class="main-content area-huntingdon-page" style="font-family: 'Poppins', Arial, sans-serif;">

    <style>
      .area-huntingdon-page {
        --area-blue: #0a1a4a;
        --area-blue-2: #162b70;
        --area-gold: #d4af37;
        --area-soft: #f5f7fb;
        --area-text: #334155;
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }
      .area-wrap { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; }
      .area-huntingdon-page section,
      .area-huntingdon-page h1,
      .area-huntingdon-page h2,
      .area-huntingdon-page h3,
      .area-huntingdon-page p,
      .area-huntingdon-page img,
      .area-huntingdon-page a { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; }
      .area-hero { padding: 112px 0 96px; color: #fff; background: radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%, rgba(212,175,55,0.24) 0%, rgba(212,175,55,0) 45%), linear-gradient(132deg, #08163d 0%, #0a1a4a 45%, #1c347f 100%); }
      .area-hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.08fr 0.92fr; gap: 40px; align-items: center; }
      .area-kicker { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,232,159,0.98); color: #0a1a4a; border-radius: 999px; padding: 10px 18px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.6px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; }
      .area-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 58px); line-height: 1.1; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 15ch; }
      .area-hero p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92); margin: 0 0 26px; max-width: 60ch; }
      .area-hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 28px; }
      .area-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; padding: 14px 24px; }
      .area-btn-primary { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffe89f 0%, #9f7628 100%); color: #111827; }
      .area-btn-ghost { color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }
      .lc-metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 8px; }
      .lc-metric { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px; text-align: center; }
      .lc-metric strong { display: block; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1; color: #ffe89f; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .lc-metric span { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.84); }
      .area-hero-card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.11); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 20px; padding: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(8px); }
      .area-hero-card img { width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; }
      .area-price { margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; color: #0a1a4a; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
      .area-price strong { color: #111827; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-section { padding: 86px 0; }
      .area-head { text-align: center; max-width: 830px; margin: 0 auto 34px; }
      .area-head h2 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 12px; }
      .area-head p { color: #475569; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }
      .area-intro { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 26px; }
      .area-panel { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e4e9f2; border-radius: 16px; padding: 24px; box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05); }
      .area-panel h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
      .area-panel p { color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 14px; }
      .area-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 9px; }
      .area-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 9px; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-list i { color: var(--area-gold); margin-top: 3px; }
      .area-types-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 18px; }
      .area-type { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; padding: 20px; }
      .area-type h3 { font-size: 21px; color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-type p { margin: 0; color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-zone { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #102559 100%); }
      .area-zone .area-head h2, .area-zone .area-head p { color: #fff; }
      .area-zone-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
      .area-zone-item { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 { color: #ffe89f; font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a { color: #ffe89f; text-decoration: none; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .area-zone-item p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
      .area-proof-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
      .area-proof { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; text-align: center; padding: 20px; }
      .area-proof i { color: var(--area-gold); font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .area-proof h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 7px; }
      .area-proof p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
      .area-faq { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-faq-grid { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
      .area-faq-item { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; }
      .area-faq-item h3 { color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-faq-item p { margin: 0; color: #334155; line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-cta { padding: 88px 0; text-align: center; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #1f3a8a 100%); }
      .area-cta h2 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); }
      .area-cta p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 24px; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px; }
      @media (max-width: 1080px) { .area-types-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-zone-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      @media (max-width: 900px) { .area-hero { padding: 86px 0 70px; } .area-hero-grid, .area-columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-hero h1 { max-width: 100%; } }
      @media (max-width: 680px) { .lc-metrics { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-section, .area-cta { padding: 64px 0; } .area-types-grid, .area-zone-grid, .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-head p, .area-hero p, .area-cta p { font-size: 16px; } }
    </style>

    <section class="area-hero">
      <div class="area-wrap area-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="area-kicker"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> Huntingdon, Cambridgeshire</span>
          <h1>Loft Conversion Huntingdon For Local Homes</h1>
          <p>Need a loft conversion in Huntingdon? We work across the full range of Huntingdon housing, from Victorian terraces in the town centre to 1970s and 1980s semis on surrounding estates. Each build is planned around your roof structure and planning situation. See our full <a href="/services/loft-conversion-cambridge-service/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Loft Conversion Service page</a> for details.</p>
          <div class="area-hero-actions">
            <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Get Free Survey <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a>
            <a href="/gallery/" class="area-btn area-btn-ghost">View Our Work</a>
          </div>
          <div class="lc-metrics">
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i></strong><span>Free Site Survey</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i></strong><span>Fully Insured</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-award"></i></strong><span>Quality Assured</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="area-hero-card">
          <img src="/wp-content/uploads/Loft-Conversion/loft-conversion-cambridge.webp" alt="Loft conversion in Huntingdon Cambridgeshire by Truleum">
          <div class="area-price">
            <span>Typical project budget</span>
            <strong>From £28,000</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-intro">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Local Approach For Every Loft Conversion In Huntingdon</h2>
          <p>We plan each Huntingdon loft conversion around your roof type, planning situation and how you need the room to function. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">homeowner guide</a> walks you through the full process from survey to completion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-columns">
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <p>Your Huntingdon loft conversion includes design input, structural build, insulation, roof windows or dormers, electrics and a high quality finish throughout.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Clear scope and fixed stage pricing</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Regular updates from survey through to handover</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Practical room layouts for bedrooms, offices and suites</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Building control support throughout the build</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>Why Huntingdon Homes Need Specialist Input</h3>
            <p>Huntingdon has a wide mix of property types. Getting a loft conversion right means understanding each roof structure, dealing with planning rules correctly and managing build logistics in residential streets. See the <a href="https://www.planningportal.co.uk/permission/common-projects/loft-conversion" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Planning Portal loft conversion rules</a> for permitted development guidance.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Experience with Huntingdon terraces, semis and detached homes</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Design solutions to maximise usable headroom</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Efficient staircase planning to protect existing floor space</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Careful build management to reduce disruption</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Popular Loft Conversion Types For Huntingdon Homes</h2>
          <p>We assess your roof and recommend the best option for your property and budget. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">glossary</a> explains each type in plain language.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-types-grid">
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Dormer Conversion</h3>
            <p>Most popular choice for Huntingdon terraces and semis. Creates strong headroom and usable floor area for bedrooms, ensuites and home offices.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Velux Conversion</h3>
            <p>A cost effective option using roof windows. Suits homes where budget is a priority or where minimal changes to the roofline are preferred.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Hip To Gable</h3>
            <p>An excellent choice for end of terrace and semi detached homes in Huntingdon. Extends the roof to create proper width and usable room proportions.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-zone">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Areas We Cover Around Huntingdon</h2>
          <p>We serve Huntingdon and the surrounding Cambridgeshire towns and villages with the same standards and clear project management on every job.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-zone-grid">
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Huntingdon Town</h3><p>Victorian terraces, interwar semis and postwar estates across the town centre and inner suburbs.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Godmanchester</h3><p>Period properties and modern housing in this historic town adjoining Huntingdon.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Brampton and Buckden</h3><p>Commuter villages with a strong mix of detached and semi detached family homes.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Hemingford Grey</h3><p>Riverside village with period cottages and modern infill development.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-st-ives-cambridgeshire/">St Ives</a></h3><p>Neighbouring market town with a large range of Victorian and modern properties.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-st-neots/">St Neots</a></h3><p>Growing town to the southwest with extensive family housing and new developments.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-ely/">Ely</a> Area</h3><p>Serving Ely and Fenland communities northeast of Huntingdon.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/">Cambridge</a></h3><p>Full Cambridge city coverage including surrounding villages and suburbs.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Why Huntingdon Homeowners Choose Truleum</h2>
          <p>We deliver reliable loft conversions across Huntingdon with transparent pricing, quality materials and strong project communication at every stage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-proof-grid">
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-map-marked-alt"></i><h3>Local Team</h3><p>Solid understanding of Huntingdon housing stock, planning rules and build logistics.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-file-signature"></i><h3>Transparent Quotes</h3><p>Detailed written quotes with clear inclusions and no surprise costs mid build.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i><h3>Fully Insured</h3><p>Complete insurance cover throughout the project for your peace of mind.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-award"></i><h3>Quality Finish</h3><p>Attention to detail at every stage delivers a loft room that feels properly complete.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-faq">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Huntingdon Loft Conversion FAQs</h2>
          <p>Common questions from Huntingdon homeowners planning a loft conversion. See our <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">2026 cost guide</a> for full pricing detail.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-faq-grid">
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How much does a loft conversion in Huntingdon cost?</h3>
            <p>Most projects in Huntingdon range from £28,000 to £62,000 depending on loft type, structural requirements and finishing level. We give a clear written quote after a free site visit.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Are semis in Huntingdon good candidates for loft conversions?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Semi detached homes in Huntingdon often suit hip to gable or dormer conversions well. The right solution depends on your specific roof structure, which we assess during the survey.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in Huntingdon?</h3>
            <p>Most standard loft conversions in Huntingdon fall under permitted development and do not need planning permission. Properties in designated areas or with major roof changes may need an application. We advise clearly on this during the survey.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How long does a Huntingdon loft conversion take?</h3>
            <p>A typical build takes between 6 and 10 weeks from start date, depending on the conversion type, structural complexity and level of specification.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-cta">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);">Useful links: <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Loft Conversion Glossary</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cost Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Homeowner Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cambridge Area Page</a></p>
        <h2>Plan Your Huntingdon Loft Conversion Today</h2>
        <p>Book a free site survey to talk through layout ideas, timeline and cost. We will help you get the most from your Huntingdon home.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Book Free Consultation <i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a loft conversion in Huntingdon cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most loft conversion projects in Huntingdon range from £28,000 to £62,000 depending on loft type, structural requirements and finishing level."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are semis in Huntingdon good candidates for loft conversions?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Semi detached homes in Huntingdon often suit hip to gable or dormer conversions well, depending on the specific roof structure."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in Huntingdon?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most standard loft conversions in Huntingdon fall under permitted development. Properties in designated areas or with major roof changes may need a planning application."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a Huntingdon loft conversion take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A typical Huntingdon loft conversion takes 6 to 10 weeks from build start, depending on conversion type and specification."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
    </script>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
